When it came to who should play the next James Bond , everyone had an opinion.

Now that the seventh Bond has been revealed as Robert Pattinson , plenty of people are sharing new opinions. We're still waiting to hear from some of the bigger names connected to the franchise but below are are some of the early reactions to the news.

The Ian Fleming Estate took to social media to congratulate the actor on his selection, saying they were &#8220;delighted to welcome Robert Pattinson to the James Bond family.&#8221;

&#8220;As Bond himself reflects at the end of Moonraker when facing the fact that the object of his affections is engaged to another man, &#8216;He must play the role which she expected of him. The tough man of the world. The Secret Agent. The man who was only a silhouette.' We look forward to Pattinson stepping into that silhouette and making it his own. We have no doubt that Ian Fleming would be amazed at the longevity of his creation and the fact that the world is still hungry for tales of the world's greatest spy. As the custodians of Ian Fleming's literary work, we wish Pattinson and everyone associated with the film the very best of luck. And as die-hard fans, we can't wait for Bond 26.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Never afraid to wade in, presenter Piers Morgan said casting Pattinson was a bad call, primarily because the actor is also starring as Batman. &#8220;Batman can't be Bond too,&#8221; Morgan wrote. &#8220;They should have gone for an unknown. Bad call.&#8221;

Christopher Hogg , Senior Lecturer in Screen Studies at the University of Westminster, had some interesting thoughts on the subject, calling it &#8220;a clear shift in casting strategy for the iconic character.&#8221;

&#8220;The announcement of Robert Pattinson as Bond marks a clear shift in casting strategy for the iconic character in the franchise's new Amazon MGM era. Whilst previous actors cast in the role had established star profiles, their fame has never been on this scale prior to donning the tuxedo and pointing the Walther PPK. Pattinson is unquestionably a talented actor with varied screen credits that demonstrate his abilities in both emotional complexity and full-throttle action. However, the background resonances of Twilight and Batman will ring loud when he reaches the screen as Bond. Pattinson's casting confirms Amazon's &#x2018;commercial metrics' approach is now being applied to Bond's screen future.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

He continued: &#8220;The choice also makes sense in terms of established working relationships, with the new Bond director Denis Villeneuve having very recently worked with Pattinson on Dune: Part Three . The casting choice certainly marks a decisive change of approach. People were very quick to criticise the casting of Daniel Craig in the first few months, however, and what followed was both critical and commercial success. Let's keep an open mind, for now.&#8221;

A number of critics and online film commentators are having their say. Online critic and YouTuber Will Jordan, known on X as The Critical Drinker , was disappointed by the casting, calling it &#8220;an odd choice. Predictable and safe in some ways (high profile, established actor) but weird in others (already 40 years old, not especially physical or masculine, and already committed to another franchise with Batman). Hmm&#8230;&#8221;

Meanwhile, as often happens, the internet is having fun with a cultural moment. Aggregation site Discussing Film points out that the Twilight movies &#8220;predicted&#8221; Pattinson's casting in a scene where a character name drops James Bond and the camera immediately cuts to Pattinson's character Edward Cullen.

